{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-\ud83d\udc7b-a-handful-of-sample-geists","id":1517001,"title":"\ud83d\udc7b A Handful of Sample Geists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-02T14:38:56-07:00","id":1517001,"title":"\ud83d\udc7b A Handful of Sample Geists","content":"\u200bAfter making a <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter the Vigil supplement</a>, I'm going to move onto my favourite game line and do something a little more ambitious. I'm going to make a Night Horrors book for Geist. And one part of that is going to be making a buttload of Geists and Sin-eaters that can be mix and matched or provide Storytellers with a toolbox for making antagonists.<br /> I've been banging away at these and really enjoying it, so I'm going to share a few of my favourites right here, as a little teaser for what's tentatively titled <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>.<br /> <br /> Each of these is given a description, which usually includes a vague idea of what they were in life, how they communicate with their Sin-eater, and what appearance they take. I then go over their mechanics. I even created a few Crisis Points for many of them. For Keys, I really felt I was using too many of a certain Key, so instead of limiting myself to not using it, I instead started giving several Keys they could take. Mechanically all of them are player ready. Last, I go over what Deathmask they create if you manage to defeat them, which shows the Reaper they create as well as the quirk that the Deathmask has when worn by someone living. I was tempted to even go so far as to give the actual stat buffs the Deathmask gives a Reaper, but I think I'll leave that up to storytellers.<br /> <br /> We'll start with something relatively simple. A ghost who had a change of heart after he rose from the dead. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/FAZJVkelgcg\" target=\"_blank\">The only thing worse than a ghost who knows he's a racist is a flesh and blood cracker who doesn't.</a> <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1248_1688330096543_539\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1248\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1248\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1248&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Rebel Son is clad in a dirty spectral grey uniform and smells of gunpowder and wet dirt. He stands at attention, his unearthly mien gaunt and hollow. He carries a rifle, battered and broken, and the field pack of one of his rank, which was actually very low. He never drank from a River, instead rising as the first victim of the battlefield.<br /> The Rebel Son is the rare ghost who changed after death, experiencing something of character growth. He died with spite in his heart, but after death he began to understand that he was part of the problem. Now saddled with guilt for his part in upholding a broken world, yet unable to interact with it to fix it, he longs for a Sin-eater who will help him make amends.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> An absolute certainty that he was doing the right thing, privilege and entitlement, terror as bullets flew through the air, shot in the heart, seeing the rotted fruits of his labors, Redlining, institutional violence, an unearthly vow he no longer keeps<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance Trait:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Firearms<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Power:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Virtue:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Justice, <b><b><b><b><b>Vice:</b></b></b></b></b> Guilt<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Hornswoggled; Being mislead and causing harm is too close to the Rebel Son\u2019s life (and Death) for comfort<br /> <b><b><b><b>Ban:</b></b></b></b> Discorporates at the sound of a bugle call; <b>Bane:</b> A Union Flag; a real one, not just some hick's tee shirt.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Kindly; <b><b><b><b>Key:</b></b></b></b> Blood \u2014 Bloody uniform, blood on his hands, Disease \u2014 It\u2019s not the bullet that gets you, it\u2019s the gangrene<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - Bigot Kepi</b><br /> In death the Rebel Son becomes everything he hated about his life. A Confederate cap drenched in blood and torn in ways that look like a tormented face, the Bigot Kepi turns a ghost into the Reaper <b>The Pogromite</b>, a monstrous embodiment of xenophobia. No longer just the Confederacy, the Reaper takes on the appearance of Cossacks and genocidaires from all over history. Their face is a grisly skull, and when they Engulf their victims, they tear the ghost to mist and suck it in.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> Like calls to like, and anyone wearing the Bigot Kepi will be able to sense animosity towards any sort of minority group. While wearing creepy Confederate hat in public might (rightly) get your ass kicked in some places, this kind of thing is useful for finding social weak points and knowing a target\u2019s bigotries and biases can be valuable.<br /> \u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now we're going to get a little weird. How about a Doppelganger as a geist? What about <i>your</i> doppelganger? This one may not make the cut because it's a little too silly and breaks the format too much, but I want to share it as part of this conga line of increasingly ridiculous concepts. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1249_1688330227799_92\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1249\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1249\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1249&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is a little embarrassing. You may not remember it, or it may just be a funny story about how you were drunk or high or simply in a bad place at a bad time, but your Bargain wasn\u2019t the first time you died. Well, maybe not died. You were mostly fine, but for just a brief moment of \u201chey ya\u2019ll, watch this\u201d or bad luck, you almost earned a Darwin award. And while most of you kept on going, you left behind a ghost. A ghost that kept on existing even though you were still alive. That ghost drank from a River, but it still knew enough about itself to seek you out specifically.<br /> Maybe it even had another Bound first that disappointed it. Either way, you didn\u2019t realize it enough, but you\u2019ve got a twin. Which one of you is the evil one, if any, is up for debate. It speaks like you, acts like you, and wants what you want. You\u2019d think that would be great for Synergy, but you\u2019re starting to suspect otherwise. Maybe you\u2019re more insufferable than you thought. And the Underworld did not change you nearly enough to mellow you out. If anything, it made you worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> You remember, right?<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance Trait:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> There\u2019s a Skill you used to care about but gave up on. Your dead self didn\u2019t.<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Six dots in your greatest category, Five dots in your second best category, four dots in your worst category<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Virtue:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Your Virtue at the time; <b><b><b><b>Vice</b></b></b></b> Your Vice at the time.<br /> <b><b><b><b>Ban:</b></b></b></b> It can\u2019t do that thing you hate; <b><b><b><b>Bane:</b></b></b></b> Your least favorite object<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b> One of your Breaking Points from when you were a Human.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Your same Burden; <b><b><b><b>Key:</b></b></b></b> Chance \u2014 Hey ya\u2019ll, watch this! Disease \u2014 That fever sure was something; Blood \u2014 You got out of that scrap with a great story; Beast \u2014 The bark was worse than the bite; Deep Water \u2014 You came up eventually, it\u2019s fine; Cold Wind \u2014 Anaphylaxis is a bitch; Pyre Flame \u2014 You learned a valuable lesson about cooking; Grave Dirt \u2014 Urbex is dangerous; Silent \u2014 Replacing the carbon monoxide filter is very important<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - The Stolen Face</b><br /> The geist of a doppelganger is the epitome of being a double. When nothing but a Deathmask this is amplified, and The Stolen Face is a shiny mirror that creates a Reaper known as <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>The Mirrorskin</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b>, which reflects back everything with a sleek silvery sheen. It tricks ghosts by taking on the appearance of their loved ones. When it Engulfs a ghost it spears them with a hand and brings them into itself.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> When worn by a living user, the Stolen Face lets you continue to steal faces. The wearer can take on the form of anyone they\u2019ve seen while wearing the mask.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Alright, that's weird and a bit silly, but how about we get big and stupid. No, bigger. And when I say stupid, I mean atavistic. A barghest is an animal ghost. Sometimes those drink from Rivers, and can become geist just as easily as a human ghost can. But not every barghest is going to be a favoured puppy or a killer lion. A lot of stuff in Geist is old, so how about something <i><b>ancient</b></i>? <div align=\"center\">\u200b<img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1250_1688330672648_529\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1250\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1250\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1250&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The jungles of the past are filled with deadly predators, most of whom have been pounded to dust by the ages. Not so of the nearly complete skeleton of an tyrannosaurus rex known as Amy. Fifteen feet of deadly predator and crushing jaws, one of the most impressive attractions at the museum. They say that you die your final death the last time you're remembered, and after aeons of silence the collective excitement of paleontologists, researchers, and <i>crowds</i> brought this beast out of slumber.<br /> The Main Exhibit is blood and bone and feathers and above all <i><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>teeth</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></i>. It is massive. It communicates in atavistic rumbling and ear splitting roars. It thinks like a predator and the Bound can only intuit the alien desires of a phantasmal monstrosity. It\u2019s a wonder it managed to grant the Bargain. But that reptile brain is now so much more aware in death, and doubly so with the sensations of the Bargain.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A brutal life, every day a struggle, the teeth and horns, years of nothing, then attention and accolades, all ending in a wooden crate and lack of funding. <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance Trait:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Survival<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b></b></b></b></b></b><br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Virtue:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Power; <b><b><b><b><b>Vice:</b></b></b></b></b> Hunger<br /> <b><b><b><b>Ban:</b></b></b></b> <i><b><b>Must</b></b></i> eat the flesh of anything it kills, and yes, this includes the Sin-eater, so pull your punches unless you\u2019re hungry and interested in cannibalism (this doesn\u2019t demand ectophagia, ghosts don\u2019t have flesh); <b><b><b><b>Bane</b></b></b></b>: The natural weapons of a prey animal (horns, hooves, tusks) anointed with the sap of an angiosperm.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Helplessness; Nothing could make nearly 15,000 kilos of muscle feel helpless, but the Main Exhibit is trapped in the meat of a Sin-eater.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Hungry; <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Suggested Keys:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Beast \u2014 The King of them; Cold Wind \u2014 The ash filled the sky and the world went cold; Grave Dirt \u2014 the weight of ages<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - The Crown of Teeth</b><br /> Considering a Tyrannosaurus Rex would be somewhere around Size 20, giving this Geist 25 Corpus, it would take a team of hunters red in tooth and claw to take down the Main Exhibit. If anyone manages that feat, they\u2019ll be rewarded with a dinosaur skull that can wear as a skull cap, regardless of what size their actual head is. A ghost who wears the Crown of Teeth becomes the most dread of Reapers. <b>Ozymandias, the King of Kings</b>. Look upon her works and despair. An only vaguely humanoid beast of tooth and feathers, they aren\u2019t as grand as the Exhibit itself, but they can still Engulf a ghost the old fashioned way: Swallowing it whole.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> When worn by a living being the Crown of Teeth becomes a weapon equivalent to a fire axe except that it uses Brawl instead of Weaponry. By spending a point of Willpower, the wearer of the Crown can bite and claw and rend, dealing the Leg or Arm Wrack tilt.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And finally, my favorite of the entire bunch so far, I wanted to really get weird (as if a dinosaur ghost wasn't pretty out there) and think of a Castoff Geist. While I'd originally been kicking around the idea of a kasa-obake or some kind of magical sword, there's nothing more iconic than the haunted house. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1251_1688331246762_657\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1251&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/mexs39y0Imw\" target=\"_blank\">In the psychology of the modern civilized human being, it is hard to overstate the significance of the house.</a> The House That Hates was not a house that was haunted <b><b><b>by</b></b></b> something. It is a house that rejects humanity. The House That Hates is what happens when a house is left alone. When it is left to wear and age. For eighty years it sat alone on a hill and alone it grew angry. Eventually it died, even without ever really being alive. The hallways began to stretch. The brickwork shifts. The doors disappeared, or lead to hallways where they should have opened to the yard. And then it was demolished. And it sank into the Underworld, but it didn\u2019t stay there.<br /> How it came to drink from a River is unknown, but it is now a Geist. To the Sin-eater, the House sprawls around them. Doors open in Twilight spaces that aren\u2019t there in reality. The wallpaper spreads like leprous lesions across walls and surfaces. In a large enough open space the House might simply take full form. It communicates with the Sin-eater through paintings and torn bloody wallpaper, though does so rarely. Warnings rip themselves into the walls and reveal themselves as foggy shadows in the mirrors that aren\u2019t there for anyone else.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> One happy family in a freshly built house. An accidental death. Grief. The family moves out. A child\u2019s ghost passes on. Loneliness. Spite. <b><i><b><b>Anger.</b></b></i><br /> Remembrance Trait:</b> By spending three Plasm, the Bound can use an effect similar to the Death Knocker's quirk (see below), except that the still 'living' consciousness of The House holds together and won't destroy anything left inside. <br /> <b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Virtue:</b> Welcoming; <b><b><b><b><b>Vice:</b></b></b></b></b> Spite<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Loneliness; The House Hates because it was abandoned. It can\u2019t stand a Bound-or world\u2014that won\u2019t interact with it, and the Bound is the only way it can interact with the world.<br /> <b><b><b>Ban</b></b></b>: While it might take over the walls in Twilight and spread itself with abandon, the House That Hates can\u2019t do anything to destroy an equally old, turn of the last century house, no matter how jealous it might be of something still loved, <b><b><b>Bane:</b></b></b> A family photo, in the frame, that\u2019s been in the same house for a decade<br /> <b>Burden:</b> Abiding; <b><b><b><b>Key:</b></b></b></b> Grave Dirt \u2014 the House stood for eighty years and might have stood for eighty more; Silent \u2014 Empty and alone, left to fester; Chance \u2014 Another\u2019s death lead to the \u2018death\u2019 of the House<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - The Death Knocker</b><br /> How do you wear a house? This brass gargoyle door knocker functions well enough as a mask, and attaches itself to the face without a problem. The Marleyan visage is unnerving enough when worn by one of the Bound, when a ghost puts it on they become Reaper <b>The Oldest House</b>. You don\u2019t wear a house, you <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>become</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> the House. The Reaper fades, their body below the Mask becoming even more ethereal than usual. When they are within a structure is when they become truly terrifying. They become the structure, the doors and hallways becoming that of the House, it\u2019s walls and rooms ancient and anachronistic. When the Oldest House Engulfs a ghost, rooms open to blackness and shadowy hands pull it in before closing tight. When a House is both hungry and awake, every room becomes a mouth.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> Worn by a Sin-eater the Death Knocker is still an unnerving plate of metal, but it provides a much less nightmarish benefit. By knocking on any standard door\u2014the kind found in offices, schools, bathrooms, or houses\u2014and using one of their Keys in the lock (regardless of what type of key it takes) the Bound can open the door into a phantom bedroom from the House before it began to Hate. It looks like it belongs to a child in the early teen years somewhere in the early 1900. The door will stay open for a number of turns equal to a character\u2019s Synergy or equivalent trait, to a minimum of zero for a mortal. Whether the mask is worn or not, the user can leave the room by imagining a door and opening it, stepping out at a compatible door somewhere else in the world. While this sounds like the perfect safehouse, anything left behind in the room when the mask leaves it is no longer there the next time the room is visited. It would take powerful magic or an epic quest to recover it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know this forum seems a bit dead, but hopefully this gets people excited for Geist. Some of the other ideas:<ul><li>A Deathmask that lets you do a Vampire's Kiss.</li> <li>The Ghost of <a href=\"https://youtu.be/GqSEAv8GItA\" target=\"_blank\">Sara Berry</a></li> <li>Santa Claus (and a Deathmask that creates <a href=\"https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-4666\" target=\"_blank\">The Yule Man</a>)</li> <li>Bloody Mary</li> <li>Ghost Rider</li> <li>Rules for Tyranny and sample Tyrants</li> <li>Ghosts that aren't ghosts, primarily household spirits and small gods like lares, zashiki-warashi, and domovoi.</li> <li>New Ghost-Eaters and Ceremonies for Necromancers</li> <li>Kerberoi and Cthonians</li> <li>Deathlords ???</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T20:23:00-07:00","id":1517027,"title":"","content":"These are interesting. I don't know that a barghest can be a Geist, but it's a cool idea none the less. Might work better as a plain old spirit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T20:40:01-07:00","id":1517028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-\ud83d\udc7b-a-handful-of-sample-geists?p=1517027#post1517027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are interesting. I don't know that a barghest can be a Geist, but it's a cool idea none the less. Might work better as a plain old spirit though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can. Or at least there's nothing saying they can't (I'd think the Castoff would be more unusual in that sense, it can't even drink!)<br /> <br /> Washington, D.C. also has Demon Cat (initials D.C.) a Barghest Geist that is Unleashed but rumored to be Bound to a Senator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T01:31:15-07:00","id":1517252,"title":"","content":"Okay, I think I've outdone myself in terms of weirdness with this one. An Exile that became a Geist. This one is actually the Geist of one of the sample Tyrants. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1285_1688631770108_433\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1285\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1285\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1285&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1286_1688702267365_335\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> There are strange things in the Chronicles of Darkness and not all of them used to be human (or house, or tyrannosaurus rex). Some of them are created for a purpose, and sometimes that purpose is left unfulfilled, abandoned, forgotten, impossible, or completed without a replacement. Angels are supposed to exist for a purpose, and Who Is Like God? was left to find a purpose of it\u2019s own. Through an unusual series of occult matrices that trigger upon the death of a human being in the presence of an entity that has drank from a River of the Underworld, it was able to find a purpose: The Bargain. Of course, experiencing life through the calculating brain, multitudinous extradimensional eyes, and glorious form of a seraphim and experiencing life through the solid fleshy meat, subjective, experiential mind, and muddy imprecise eyes of a human being. The Archangel may be in for more than it expected in this new mission it bestowed upon itself.<br /> The Archangel was not originally a ghost, but through usurping the process of the Bargain it has become one. The form it takes is a pale shadow of it\u2019s original glory, but its corpus still takes the shape of a \u201cBiblically Accurate\u201d angel. A roughly human shape with six wings of burnished brass, each covered in disturbingly human eyes. Instead of a human face, it has a halo of bone, the rim of which is also tipped with eyes. The gown it wears flows into the void, but a tabard adorns it with symbols written in unknown language and trimmed with gold. From its\u2019 corpus it produces a flaming sword. It communicates with the Bound through the sound of trumpets, distant at best but never quiet. It bears a deep grudge against those it calls Demons, but through the act of drinking from a River and the Bargain itself, it only has a hazy notion of what this even means.<br /> <br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Being formed by holy fire within the crucible of god with a mission, the mission that could never be fulfilled, confusion that should not be possible, drinking from the River to better serve Him. Is this really the path?<br /> <b>Remembrance Trait:</b> Occult<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Virtue:</b></b></b></b></b></b> Dedication, <b><b><b><b><b>Vice:</b></b></b></b></b> Compassion<br /> <b><b><b><b>Ban:</b></b></b></b> Cannot enter religious buildings without express permission (the hours of a service count, office hours don\u2019t), <b><b><b><b><b>Bane:</b></b></b></b></b> A religious relic that has been profaned.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Chaos; Who Is Like God? does not function well when there\u2019s confusion. Not having a clear goal or mission sends it into panic.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Abiding, though Who Is Like God? never died; <b>Suggested Keys:</b> Pyre Flame - Holy holy holy holy! Chance - If God doesn\u2019t make mistakes, what happened?<br /> <br /> <b><b>Deathmask - The Face of the Fallen</b></b><br /> This is a thing that should not be. A piece of an angel. A dead angel. And yet here it is. It\u2019s almost too normal of a Deathmask. A domino mask made of brass feathers, each with a dull, milky white unblinking eye. It covers the wearer\u2019s actual eyes, but that doesn\u2019t matter because you can see through the dead ones. When worn they tend to writhe about wherever the wearer is looking. When a ghost puts on the Face of the Fallen they become Samael, <b>The Poison of God</b>. A thing of shadows and crow feathers, and broken, rusted machinery. Their fingers are stained black with machine oil, and it leaks from their eyes. When they Engulf, the offending ghost is pounced upon by those wings, and when the fluttering stops and Samael stands, the ghost is gone.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Wearing the Face allows you to see the hidden gears and pullies that pervade reality. Some spaces are larger than they are for others, hiding entire structures within alleyways. Strange spiders and other mechanical creatures lurk within these structures. But being able to see the Infrastructure isn\u2019t actually the quirk of the Face of the Fallen. That would be ability to craft an entirely different life. When the Face is worn, the wearer can cobble together a different life for themselves. When wearing the Face of the Fallen for the first time, craft a Cover by rearranging your Social Merits however you like (don\u2019t include any free dots from the likes of Mystery Cult). The Cover is a completely new person, and can even be of a different gender, ethnicity, or even supernatural type, though you still have your existing powers. After wearing the mask for a scene, you have access to this additional life, which includes a history and identifying documents and you even exist within the memories of other people. If ever something comes up where you\u2019re pressed and don\u2019t actually have the abilities that your Cover should have, roll a Clash of Wills. Success means you can fake it. Living in the alternate life for more than twelve hours within a day is a Breaking Point or the equivalent. The life doesn\u2019t actually need your constant upkeep, and will go on without you, and when you acquire a new dot of Social merit in your real life, your Cover gains an equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 07-06-2023, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T07:58:48-07:00","id":1517356,"title":"","content":"really looking forward to this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T04:04:08-07:00","id":1517551,"title":"","content":"Got some more things to show off. Starting with mechanics for Tyranny. Just the bullet points for now, still hammering out the actual section writing. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1287_1688899952833_224\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1287\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1287\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1287&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Intimate Knowledge:</b> The first step towards Tyranny is to know your Geist\u2019s Touchstone (usually by reaching Synergy 3).</li> <li><b>Flatline:</b> Tyranny can only be attempted while Flatlining, whether intentionally caused by the Tyrant or naturally occurring.</li> <li><b>Touchstone Destruction:</b> A Tyrant must perform a ceremonial destruction of the Geist\u2019s Touchstone. Doing so causes a Crisis Point, and through banes the Tyrant can subdue their geist. If the geist manages to intercede in defense of the Touchstone, it may not be able to hurt the Bound but it can still allow a living Touchstone to flee or manage to hide an object Touchstone. This is only a temporary solution.</li> <li><b>Dread Presence:</b> A Tyrant\u2019s Liminal Aura bestows the Shaken Condition (if fear might hinder a roll, choose to take a failure and resolve Shaken instead; the *Storyteller* can choose when to resolve the Tyrant\u2019s Shaken Condition if you don\u2019t).</li> <li><b>Truly Bound:</b> A Tyrant\u2019s geist bears visible chains of red veined silver. Anyone capable of seeing ghostly Twilight is able to see this, and while the effect comes with a level of supernatural comprehension of \u201cthis is bad\u201d, the specifics aren\u2019t easy to figure out without context. When a Tyrant\u2019s geist is Unleashed, whether from a Crisis Point or the Tyrant\u2019s death, the chains can be broken, freeing the Geist and killing the Tyrant permanently.</li> <li><b>Oppressive:</b> Tyrants roll Tyranny+Intimidate to control their Geist during a Crisis Point so long as they let their geist Unleashed once a week. Tyrants usually create warded saferooms for this period.</li> <li><b>Samsara:</b> Upon final death, a Tyrant rises as a Guardian Geist incapable of remembering their life and their corpse blooms into an ironic display of life from death. Within a week, an Avernian Gate will form.</li> <li><b>Synergistic:</b> In all other ways, such as Clash of Wills or activating Haunts, Tyranny functions as Synergy. Tyranny is still lost on Death or the creation of a Memento, but not on forcing a Geist to drink from a River (and as such the path of Tyranny is perfect for Bound attempting Cabairos) or committing Ectophagia.</li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd now a Sample Tyrant, though I haven't gotten around to making the character sheet for him. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1288_1688900107434_229\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1288\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1288\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1288&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Simon Meletis was a man with no prospects. He was raised Catholic, and even went to seminary, but lost his faith after the death of his child and shortly after his wife. He barely remembers those days anymore, though. At his lowest point, Simon was willing to take his own life. He went to a bridge at night and stared into the dark waters below. An Angel was there with him, but this wasn\u2019t Clarence come to talk him out of it. If anything, Who Is Like God? was encouraging him to jump. It was the aftermath that the Archangel cared about. While Simon was there in the inky black, his life stolen away, the Angel offered him a second chance at life. A second chance to avoid Hell for committing the gravest sin and taking a life without the possibility of repentance and redemption. All it would cost was to eternally dedicate his Soul to God. Of course, Simon would eventually come to understand that his soul was already forfeit and in his own mind eternally bound for Hell, but he considers this a pernicious lie.<br /> <br /> For a while, he was a good Sin-eater. He did good deeds and helped ghosts pass on. But as his Synergy climbed, Who Is Like God? wanted him to focus more and more on rooting out \u201cDemons\u201d. Unfortunately, the Angel wasn\u2019t particularly clear on what that meant. The Angel even swore that it was demonic forces that had taken the lives of his family, stolen them from him. Whether it was true or not, Simon was eventually convinced. He began preaching against the Demons, the shadowy forces behind the world. Blood sucking monsters. Witches who manipulated the laws of nature. Shamanistic shapeshifters in league with the devil. Pagan faeries. Reanimated monsters trying to infiltrate humanity. Necromancers summoning demons from the pit. In short, Meletis had found his demons: Every supernatural other than himself. And people began to follow him. Drawn by the things he had to say. After all, what supernatural hasn\u2019t made enemies among mortals? Vampires prey on the vulnerable and weak willed, Changelings play with mortal emotions, Sleepers are nothing but pawns to many Mages, and so on. The Lambs of God is made up of the ranks of victims and surviving family members. All willing to listen to Father Simon and help finance his crusade. The inner circle were even willing to kill for him.<br /> <br /> After a while, Who Is Like God? was outpaced in fervor. The Angel was not as bloodthirsty as Meletis would have liked, and he came to see it as God\u2019s will to subjugate the Angel, wrestling with it as Israel once did. He engaged in the process of Tyranny and chained the Archangel to himself, taking on the new name of Michaelangelo. This is only a name that he takes on when he dons the mantle of Sword of God, taking on the krewe\u2019s Regalia. He is the *only* one granted that right, though his krewe as a whole are ready to kill (or die) for Michaelangelo. They fully believe that the world needs to be cleansed of demonic forces.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Father Simon is a tall man, and dominates any room he\u2019s a part of through sheer size. He wears the robes of a priest, though he isn\u2019t actually ordained, and his teachings are *extremely* heterodox. He has tattoos from his time as a Sin-eater, as well as before he went to seminary school when he was more of a troublemaker. His entire back is taken up by a mural of Guido Reni\u2019s <i>Michael</i>. Despite his double life, when he isn\u2019t preaching fire and brimstone and the need for vigilance, Father Simon is a gentle and compassionate man who cares for everyone around him, especially children. But in a way the persona of Father Michael is an act. When he dons the Regalia and becomes Michaelangelo, he becomes a different person. He\u2019s harder, and emotionless. He wears a loose outfit based on the armor of a crusader. A tunic similar to the one Who Is Like God? wears, a single gauntleted arm. He carries a two handed sword that he\u2019s fully capable of using one handed.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Advice:</b> Michaelangelo is fucking insane. He is a quiet kind of insane. And I don\u2019t mean that he is mentally ill, I mean that he is criminally insane. The man belongs in Arkham. He has a mission and is dead set on accomplishing it. This is a man so consumed by what he sees as his God given purpose that he\u2019s willing to shackle an Angel in order to better accomplish it. He lives every waking moment of his life thinking of how to kill creatures that by their natures are difficult to kill. And the presence of his Krewe simply reinforces his beliefs that the unholy must be purged from his city, if not the world.<br /> <br /> Michaelangelo was originally created by my collaborator for a shared crossover setting where a Rapture style event occurred and the ways into and out of the city were mysteriously cut off. The game unfortunately fell apart, as these things often do, before Michaelangelo and the Lambs of God were even introduced, but he was intended to be something of a heavy arc long antagonist, with his Krewes believing that the biblical tribulation was happening and that it was a sign that they must kill the demons to bring about a paradise. The final confrontation would have been the players and the crossover allies they made facing off against The Lambs of God as they performed a ceremony to create a gate to the Lower Depths, unleashing the actual demons of Hell upon the city, under the belief that they would obey Michaelangelo\u2019s command as they once obeyed Solomon's. I strongly encourage the use of this plot, in the hopes that at least someone get some use out of it.<br /> <br /> Storytellers with Hunter: the Vigil will notice similarities between the Lambs of God and the Tribulation Militia. This is intentional, and in the above scenario most of the members of the Long Night in Ashcroft during the Cataclysm joined the Lambs of God. If you want to be extra fucking evil, you can also give Michaelangelo the Slasher template as an Avenger with a Tell of leaving E 22:18 at the site of the execution. I know technically a supernatural can\u2019t be a slasher but I don\u2019t actually care, and you shouldn\u2019t either (although that is super fucking evil). Upgrade him to a Legend before the final confrontation. Your players are Sin-eaters, they can die a few times if need be. And I mean if you\u2019re already using Hunter, feel free to give the Lambs of God Benediction.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> And if you thought a haunted house and a tyrannosaurus were a bit 'out there', here's one that's <i>really</i> wild. I've even now dedicated a whole section to what I'm calling &quot;Strange Geists&quot; that aren't simply dead humans. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1289_1688900321320_834\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1289\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1289\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1289&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There are strange things in the Chronicles of Darkness and not all of them used to be human (or house, or tyrannosaurus rex). Some of them are created for a purpose, and sometimes that purpose is left unfulfilled, abandoned, forgotten, impossible, or completed without a replacement. Angels are supposed to exist for a purpose, and Who Is Like God? was left to find a purpose of it\u2019s own. Through an unusual series of occult matrices that trigger upon the death of a human being in the presence of an entity that has drank from a River of the Underworld, it was able to find a purpose: The Bargain. Of course, experiencing life through the calculating brain, multitudinous extradimensional eyes, and glorious form of a seraphim and experiencing life through the solid fleshy meat, subjective, experiential mind, and muddy imprecise eyes of a human being. The Archangel may be in for more than it expected in this new mission it bestowed upon itself.<br /> The Archangel was not originally a ghost, but through usurping the process of the Bargain it has become one. The form it takes is a pale shadow of it\u2019s original glory, but its corpus still takes the shape of a \u201cBiblically Accurate\u201d angel. A roughly human shape with six wings of burnished brass, each covered in disturbingly human eyes. Instead of a human face, it has a halo of bone, the rim of which is also tipped with eyes. The gown it wears flows into the void, but a tabard adorns it with symbols written in unknown language and trimmed with gold. From its corpus it produces a flaming sword. It communicates with the Bound through the sound of trumpets, distant at best but never quiet. It bears a deep grudge against those it calls Demons, but through the act of drinking from a River and the Bargain itself, it only has a hazy notion of what this even means.<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Being formed by holy fire within the crucible of god with a mission, the mission that could never be fulfilled, confusion that should not be possible, drinking from the River to better serve Him. Is this really the path?<br /> <b>Touchstone:</b> The Infrastructure it was born in.<br /> <b>Remembrance Trait:</b> Unseen Sense (All) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Dedication, <b>Vice:</b> Compassion<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot enter religious buildings without express permission (the hours of a service count, office hours don\u2019t), <b>Bane:</b> A religious relic that has been profaned.<br /> <b>Crisis Point:</b> Chaos; Who Is Like God? does not function well when there\u2019s confusion. Not having a clear goal or mission sends it into panic.<br /> <b>Burden:</b> Abiding, though Who Is Like God? never died; <b>Suggested Keys:</b> Pyre Flame - Holy holy holy holy! Chance - If God doesn\u2019t make mistakes, what happened?</div> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> And I can't create a Geist without creating their Deathmask, so here's that. <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1290_1688900503170_28\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> \u200b <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is a thing that should not be. A piece of an angel. A dead angel. And yet here it is. It\u2019s almost too normal of a Deathmask. A domino mask made of brass feathers, each with a dull, milky white unblinking eye. It covers the wearer\u2019s actual eyes, but that doesn\u2019t matter because you can see through the dead ones. When worn they tend to writhe about wherever the wearer is looking. When a ghost puts on the Face of the Fallen they become <b>Samael, The Poison of God</b>. A thing of shadows and crow feathers, and broken, rusted machinery. Their fingers are stained black with machine oil, and it leaks from their eyes. When they Engulf, the offending ghost is pounced upon by those wings, and when the fluttering stops and Samael stands, the ghost is gone.<br /> <b>Quirk:</b> Wearing the Face allows you to see the hidden gears and pullies that pervade reality. Some spaces are larger than they are for others, hiding entire structures within alleyways. Strange spiders and other mechanical creatures lurk within these structures. But being able to see the Infrastructure isn\u2019t actually the quirk of the Face of the Fallen. That would be ability to craft an entirely different life. When the Face is worn, the wearer can cobble together a different life for themselves. When wearing the Face of the Fallen for the first time, craft a Cover by rearranging your Social Merits however you like (don\u2019t include any free dots from the likes of Mystery Cult). The Cover is a completely new person, and can even be of a different gender, ethnicity, or even supernatural type, though you still have your existing powers. After wearing the mask for a scene, you have access to this additional life, which includes a history and identifying documents and you even exist within the memories of other people. If ever something comes up where you\u2019re pressed and don\u2019t actually have the abilities that your Cover should have, roll a Clash of Wills (Highest Power Attribute+Occult for mortals). Success means you can fake it. Living in the alternate life for more than twelve hours within a day is a Crisis Point or the equivalent. The life doesn\u2019t actually need your constant upkeep, and will go on without you, and when you acquire a new dot of Social merit in your real life, your Cover gains an equivalent.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  What are you, a cop? 07-09-2023, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T04:38:08-07:00","id":1517553,"title":"","content":"Let's share two of the non-Tyrant Sin-eaters I've got so far, as well as two Geists to show off how things can be mix and matched. While these could be used as player characters, they're intended for Storyteller use primarily, so I've given them Synergy \u25c9\u25c9 to start with, Professional Training \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, and 20 Experiences, which is actually what I tend to give players in my games to start with. Honestly I might even throw a fourth dot of Haunt at them and five dots of Ceremonies. I love a well rounded character, and it'd also give me an excuse to make up some new Ceremonies. I'm also treating Archetype as more of a personal thing, since I prefer a Krewe where the celebrants have different roles instead of single archetype krewes. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1293_1688901503121_799\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1293\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1293\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1293&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b\u200b</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Young Daryl Friedman knew two things from an early age: One, she wanted to be a girl. And two, ever since the day her parents took her to Salem, she knew she wanted to be a witch. It was less than a year later when her parents let her dress as a witch for a Halloween party. Heading to that party is where her life changed forever. It was raining, and the truck in front of the family van slipped. Spears of metal fell out the back, stabbing her through her body. Her parents died instantly. She was still alive, and died in the hospital of infection. That\u2019s when her Geist came to her, and offered her a second chance. To live the life that she couldn\u2019t. It\u2019s been a dozen or more years since that fateful day, and Sabrina Granger now lives her childhood dream of being a witch. After all, if you\u2019re going to transition you shouldn\u2019t be boring, and if you\u2019re down in the dirt of the graveyard performing occult rituals, you might as well dress the part. She\u2019s been doing this supernatural bullshit for a long time, and has ties not just with krewes but cabals and covens and motleys and more. She also works, on a word-of-mouth basis, as a freelance problem solver for all kinds of supernatural problems, not just the ghostly ones. As if being queer wasn\u2019t enough to make foster homes hard, her \u201cimaginary friend\u201d was also a powerful ghost. Being homeless is a lot more comfortable when you\u2019re capable of magic and have someone older to watch out for you, even if that older person is dead. She can make quite a bit of money from her various odd jobs and exorcisms, she still tends to just live in the abandoned house with her cenote. While she goes by Sabrina Granger (a combination of two famous pop culture witches, though even without much in the way of an internet presence she is unfortunately aware of the associations of the surname) that\u2019s really just an alias. She doesn\u2019t really have proper documents, which is why she tends to stick to the spooky side of things and pay cash when she needs to.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Appearance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Sabrina is a teenage witch. Or, at least, the estradiol injections certainly help her look like she still is, but it\u2019s been about a decade since that was actually true. Whenever possible she dresses in a silky white blouse\u2014the Suicide Shirt\u2014and a black skirt with black and orange stripped stockings, as well as a pair of mary janes (plasm is great at getting rid of blisters). Perched on her head, and one of the most obvious trademarks to find her by, is a floppy, wide brimmed conical hat. She walks with a broom, using it as a cane. Eschewing a purse, she carries her belongings in a fancy belt pouch, a glorified fanny pack grabbed from a RenFaire, or maybe made by a lover. Beyond the witch aesthetic, one of the most notable things about her is that she\u2019s buff and has scarification tattoos. Feel free to make those Mementos if you like. Much as she enjoys the aesthetic, sometimes it needs to be ditched, such as when spelunking in the Underworld. In those cases she keeps the hat and broom (it\u2019s functional, considering the gnarled mess of flesh at her right hip), but trades her skirt and stockings for something more sensible, like jeans or even multipocketed cargo shorts. Since the cold rarely bothers her, she\u2019ll keep the blouse. Aside from being fashionable, it\u2019s bullet proof after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Advice:</b> Sabrina is either jaded or confident, depending on your outlook. She\u2019s definitely not seen it all, no one ever could. But she\u2019s sure seen a lot. She\u2019s experienced with the Chronicles of Darkness and knows enough to be valuable to any krewe that wants to seek out her information. She\u2019s also got a lot of fingers in a lot of pies. Socially, she\u2019s very friendly. She genuinely cares about people, and even if she might put on a show of frustration, she\u2019ll go to bat to help someone in need. Of course, the flip side of this is that she also is very willing to lay the hurt on the people that she thinks deserves it, usually the ones who want to take advantage of their positions of power. She has enough experience to have formed stereotypes, even if she knows they don\u2019t always hold true. Wizards are secretive, vampires are doublecrossing, faeries are always tricky with their words. She\u2019s also been around long enough to have crossed paths on friendly or not so friendly terms with all kinds of spooks, which gives plenty of ground for crossovers. As a queer in her late twenties, she\u2019s <i>also</i> been around long enough to have slept with plenty of those supernaturals, and while she gets along well enough with her flings and exes, there\u2019s always plenty of drama to be had. Isn\u2019t there always? Despite her friendliness, Sabrina doesn\u2019t have any official krewe, though she does have a loose affiliation with Frank Rook and Joy Devivre. The three know each other and sometimes work together. Depending on how you like crossover, she\u2019ll also be well known at a cafe frequented by supernatural patrons called Storybrooke.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sabrina is my own OC, and I\u2019ve mostly used her for writing character fics more than any of my other characters (It\u2019s only because the input form only allowed enough room for my first <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> character that Sabrina wasn\u2019t one of my middle names). I made her about ten years ago, and I honestly forgot about her for about four or five years until I started transitioning myself and decided to dress like a witch. I actually retroactively made Sabrina trans, since I\u2019d mostly played her as a cis woman. None of that matters, but I felt like telling the story. Your Sabrina is going to be different no matter what. But there\u2019s a reason she\u2019s getting more wordcount than anyone of the other Bound here.</div></div> </div> </div></div> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Touchstone:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Murder Weapon (Dad\u2019s Keys) - Sabrina carries her father\u2019s car keys, complete with a little plastic fob, smeared with blood. On one side is a kitschy witch advertising Salem, and on the other is a picture of young Sabrina in her own witch outfit that mom made her.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burdens:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Sabrina works best as <i>Abiding</i>, after all she was young and barely got to make a name for herself. <i>Vengeful</i> is another option, experiencing unjust circumstances leading her to protect others. <i>Bereaved</i> is good if you want to focus on the loss of her loved ones, and preventing others from experiencing that loss. This sheet is for a <b><b><b><b>Vengeful</b></b></b></b> Sabrina.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Archetype:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Sabrina fits best as a <i>Mourner</i> or <i>Pilgrim</i>, looking after the dead or helping the living deal with their grief. But with her sense of justice, she\u2019s also great as a <i>Fury</i>. A more cynical version might be a <i>Bonepicker</i>, making herself comfortable with the spoils of the dead. As a <i>Gatekeeper</i>, she would keep the living from harming or interfering with the dead.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Suggested Geists:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Sabrina was made for the Wicked Witch, who she affectionately refers to as Grandmother in my own usage. The Great Fantasmo would also fit the witch gimmick, and a Haunted House is absolutely great and would give a homeless girl somewhere to live (so feel free to change the Cenote for a Ceremony). Her vibe doesn\u2019t need to be tied to the Geist, but something with a competing aesthetic such as Senior Medianoches or Father Winter might not be good. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Intelligence \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Strength \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Presence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Wits \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Dexterity \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Manipulation \u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Resolve \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Stamina \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Composure \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> </table></div> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Synergy \u25c9\u25c9\u25c9; Keys:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> <i>Disease</i>, Silent, Blood, Geist\u2019s Key<br /> Investigation \u25cf\u25cf, \u203bOccult (Rituals) \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Athletics \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, \u203bBrawl (Rage) \u25cf, Larceny (Lockpicking) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Stealth \u25cf\u25cf, Survival \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Empathy \u25cf\u25cf, Intimidation \u25cf, Persuasion \u25cf\u25cf, \u203bStreetwise (Supernaturals, Homeless) \u25cf\u25cf<br /> \u203bdenotes an asset skill<br /> <b><b><b><b><b>Root:</b></b></b></b></b> Pollyanna, <b>Bloom:</b> Antihero<br /> <b>Haunts:</b> Memoria \u25cf, Rage \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Merits:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Memento (Suicide Shirt) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, *Manic States \u25cf, Retribution \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Safe Place+Cenote \u25cf\u25cf, Deathmask (Lover\u2019s Lips) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Area of Expertise (Rage) \u25cf, Hardy \u25cf; <b>Contacts:</b> Queers, Occultists<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 3/3, *<b>Defense:</b> 3/5, <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Initiative:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> +5, *<b>Speed:</b> 6/11, <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> *Sabrina suffers from the Leg Wrack Tilt as a Condition and gains a Beat when it causes her trouble. Numbers after the slash show the use of Manic States.<br /> <b>Suicide Shirt (Silent Key):</b> Once there was a lonely gay kid who wasn\u2019t accepted. He took his own life and his parents argued about whose fault it was (both of theirs). Sabrina jumped in the coffin before the dirt was filled and gave him last rights, then unceremoniously tore out the lining and turned it into a set of three peasant blouses. It provides 1/2 armor and the Silent Key. It also increases the Social Impression by one due to it\u2019s pleasant smell: roses and a hint of cloves.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Lover\u2019s Lips (Blood Key):</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A long time ago a courtesan fell in love with a wealthy lover and began dreaming of marriage. Just one complication: he already had a wife. He strangled her with her own scarf, and when she found her way to the Underworld she drank from the Erish-ki-gala she returned to the living and tried to unite \u2018lovers\u2019. Sabrina put an end to her efforts to bring abusers and their victims together, reducing her to a scarf with the impression of a face. Worn around the face folded down to show only the lips, you could walk down the street covered in blood and wouldn\u2019t suffer social penalties.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> And while I mention other Geists like The Great Fantasmo, The House That Hates (as above), Senior Medianoches, and Father Winter, The Wicked Witch is the &quot;canon&quot; choice for Sabrina. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1292_1688901453470_708\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1292\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1292\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1292&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Well before the events in Salem, Germany had several witch trial hysterias across the late 1500s and early 1600s. Women were burned at the stake and subjected to other similar methods of murder and torture. The Wicked Witch wasn\u2019t from Trier, Fulda, W\u00fcrzburg, or Bamberg. But she was from that area, in the Black Forest. Perhaps she was a real witch, or perhaps she was simply unfairly maligned. Either way, she was dragged the the pyre and sent to the Underworld. There she wandered adrift and finally took to one of the Rivers to drink from it. The Witch looks exactly like you\u2019d think. Green skinned and evil looking, dressed all in black with an alewife\u2019s hat. When she gets angry, her skin blackens and chars, the skin glowing through cracks. Her fingers are black from ash. She communicates in sensation, and longs to feel the sensations of humanity again. She\u2019s an <i><b>old</b></i> ghost. But even as spiteful and petty as she is, she still has a healer\u2019s heart, and wants to do good for others.<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Birthing children, providing abortifacients, minor rites for good health, communing with the spirits for protection. Mass hysteria, those she healed harming her. Dragged to the pyre. Swearing revenge.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Touchstone:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Her youngest descendant<br /> <b>R</b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>emembrance Trait:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Choose a number of Ceremonies up to three total dots.<br /> <b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Virtue:</b> Generosity, <b>Vice:</b> Spite<br /> <b>Crisis Point:</b> Betrayal; The ones she loved and nursed and healed killed her.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Apotropaics (symbols and wards against evil magic; a crucifix or magen david is too ubiquitous and won\u2019t work, unless consciously considered a holy symbol and wielded as such by someone with Integrity 8 or similar trait);<b><b><b><b><b>Bane:</b></b></b></b></b> Rowanwood<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Abiding, <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Suggested Keys:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Pyre Flame - the flames still burn within, Chance - the key of magic<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - The Witch\u2019s Hat</b><br /> A ratty alewife\u2019s hat with a pointed tip and an angry face that seems made from the folds. When worn by a ghost, they become cloaked in black and shrouded in darkness, taking on the form of <b>The Salem Shadow</b>. When they Engulf a ghost, they simply move their shadow over them and they vanish.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> When worn by a full fleshed person, the Witch\u2019s Hat grants the power of potion making. Once per chapter, with Availability \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf worth of ingredients and an hours work, you can perform a Create Equipment action to make a potion that downgrades Lethal damage equal to the equipment bonus, causes Sick or Poison (mild at -3 to the roll, grave at -5) or bottles one supernatural ability you know to allow it to be used by someone else.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1294_1688902165195_459\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1294\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1294\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1294&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">All Cops are Bastards, and Frank was a great example of this for even the best intentioned ones. He liked to think of himself as One of the Good Ones\u2122, but he definitely ignored the bad ones. When it came to getting things done, he was the best. Which when you\u2019re a cop that means you\u2019re going to break or ignore the law that already barely means shit to you. Frank was a cop in the mold of Benson Stabler. Sure, he hurt people, sometimes ones who didn\u2019t do a damned thing wrong, but he got his man. Unless he broke their wrist in questioning. He was a man with a lot of anger, even if he thought he was doing it for a good reason, and didn\u2019t give a shit about the ends so long as the means justified them. The victims needed him to help them, even if laws and limbs were broken. He was also a chain smoker, just to add to the stereotype, that\u2019ll become relevant in a bit.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If you were wondering who the character who beat out Sabrina for one of my middle names, that\u2019d be Juste, the first Chronicles of Darkness character I played. He bargained with an Acamoth to get his ex-partner a Geist sealed away in a coke bottle at the bottom of the lake, way back in 2009. Of course, that was a terrible idea back then. Will this time turn out better?</div></div> </div> </div></div> <br /> Frank also had a partner for a while. A younger, naive guy who really was idealistic. There\u2019s no Good Cop\u2122, but damn, Juste was close. And when he took a bullet to the head he saw the Watchtower of Stygia and took his skills to a private detective agency. That\u2019s about when Frank got worse. He was too much of a piece of shit to ever admit it, but he loved Juste. But Juste still kept in touch, and when he found out Frank was dying of cancer, he wanted to help. To really highlight the irony, it wasn\u2019t even lung cancer, it was a brain tumor. Maybe that\u2019s where all the anger came from. Either way, Juste wanted to help, and he came to a dying Frank and popped the cork on a bottle, introducing him to his Geist. Frank took the Bargain, but he didn\u2019t take it well, and would have died again throwing himself in front of a bus if not for the infusion of Plasm.<br /> <br /> While he lay in that hospital bed, Frank had been fully ready to die. He even realized that on almost every level, he <i><b><b><b><b>deserved</b></b></b></b></i> it, even if he had done plenty of good. Too much of it was in spite of his actions or fully by accident. If he was going to have a new lease on life, he was going to earn that second chance and do right by people. Admittedly, he\u2019s fully ready to lay the hurt if he needs to. There are too many people\u2014like his old self\u2014who don\u2019t care who they hurt in pursuit of their goals, even when they\u2019re ostensibly noble ones. Of course, he also wasn\u2019t going to go into this new world blind. He didn\u2019t listen to Juste way back when he first started all the occult detective bullshit, but now Frank was going to find all the weird shit he could and learn about it. Along the way he sort of became an expert on artifacts, fetishes, tokens, and other sorts of magical doodads and relics. He deals them on the side.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Appearance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Frank looks like Columbo if Columbo was an asshole. A shabby coat and either white collared shirts with stains on them, or random tee shirts, most of which barely fit his attitude, but they were free. Jeans instead of slacks, with the cuffs rolled up. He has that permanently stubbled look, and half the time he\u2019s sleeping in his clothes. He looks like John Constantine, in a bad way. Sting or Matt Ryan, not Keanu Reeves. Frank is almost always carrying some kind of tool box or utility belt (the same kind Sabrina, above, wears on missions). He\u2019s probably got a Memento or Artifact at hand. These days his allies finally got him to quit smoking (easy to shrug off Addiction with plasm), but he still keeps a pack and a lighter, just in case.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Storytelling Advice:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Frank is an asshole, but he\u2019s the kind of asshole who knows what he is. He\u2019s trying to be better, but when you\u2019re a supernatural bastard you\u2019re still going to cause problems. He\u2019s all in on trying to be better than he was before. His past misdeeds might come to bite him in the ass. A suspect he swore was guilty who ends up suffering because of it. Or maybe a suspect he let get away because of his off the book methods. Of course, there\u2019s also his relationship with the wizard Juste. But Frank\u2019s most obvious way of getting into a story is through his job as an \u201cantiques\u201d broker, whether it\u2019s Mementos or things from other Chronicles of Darkness gamelines. He could even show up in a game that isn\u2019t Sin-eaters, if you want to bring in something weird for a game of Vampire or Changeling. But he\u2019s not really trusting, and definitely prefers to feel a client out (usually with Sabrina\u2019s insistence) before he makes an actual deal. As a relic dealer, he\u2019s not the type to care about money (though he does still need to put food on the table), but swapping relics or getting information he knows might be valuable is worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Touchstone:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Albatross (Juste) - Juste knows everything about Frank, and most of the horrible things he\u2019s done in service of the greater good. The worst part is that he doesn\u2019t even care, he still believes that Frank is worthwhile and valuable. It\u2019s the most insufferable thing ever and even if Frank were emotionally well adjusted enough to admit his feelings, he doesn\u2019t feel worthy of that grace.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burdens:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Frank is clearly textbook <i>Kindly</i>, but he could be <i>Abiding.</i> Wanting to leave a legacy that undermines what he left before. Archetype: Like with Burden, Frank is pretty good as a <i>Fury</i>. A <i>Mourner</i> is also a good fit. For a less Sin-eater focused Frank, a more moral <i>Thanatologist</i> is fitting.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Suggested Geist:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> The Detective On Leather Wings and his unique situation are the intended Geist for Frank. But any ghost whose presence makes him feel guilty is a good choice. Zashiki-warashi is a great choice to twist the knife. The Survivor may not want to choose him, but stranger things have happened, and being trapped in a coke bottle can make you desperate. Senior Medianoches pairs well with Frank\u2019s desire to do better. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Intelligence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Strength \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Presence \u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Wits \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Dexterity \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Manipulation \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Resolve \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Stamina \u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Composure \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> </tr> </table></div> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Synergy \u25c9\u25c9; Keys:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> <i>Chance</i>, Pyre Flame, Silent, Beast, Geist\u2019s Key<br /> \u203bInvestigation (Crime Scenes) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Computers \u25cf\u25cf, Crafts (Relics) \u25cf\u25cf, \u203bOccult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Politics \u25cf<br /> Athletics (Chases) \u25cf\u25cf, Drive \u25cf, Brawl \u25cf\u25cf, \u203bFirearms (Pistols) \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Empathy \u25cf\u25cf, Intimidation (Threats) \u25cf\u25cf, Streetwise \u25cf\u25cf, Socialize \u25cf<br /> \u203bdenotes an asset skill<br /> <b><b><b><b><b>Root:</b></b></b></b></b> Cowl, <b><b><b><b><b><b>Bloom:</b></b></b></b></b></b> Saved<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Haunts:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Dirge \u25cf\u25cf, Tomb \u25cf, Shroud \u25cf<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Merits:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> *Imbued Item (Eyes of the Magi) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Area of Expertise+Interdisciplinary Specialty (Relics) \u25cf\u25cf, Reconciler \u25cf\u25cf, *Token (Filcher\u2019s Eye) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, *Talen (The House Key) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf; <b>Contacts:</b> \u201cAntique\u201d Dealers, Criminals<br /> *Frank has a number of relics that might seem familiar to troupes with access to other gamelines. Here they\u2019re all treated as unusual Mementos, and grant an appropriate Key.<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5, <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Initiative:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> +6, <b><b><b><b><b><b>Speed:</b></b></b></b></b></b> 10, <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Eyes of the Magi (Pyre Flame Key):</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A gift from Juste, these colored sunglasses allow the wearer to concentrate and better understand supernatural phenomena. Wearing them allows Frank to roll Wits+Occult (with his +2 from Relic specialty) and ask one of the following questions:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>What familiar supernatural phenomena or entity is this related to?</li> <li>What is the intended function of this relic?</li> <li>How can the relic be activated?</li> <li>How supernaturally powerful was the creator of this relic, or of the phenomena that created it?</li> <li>What mystical signature does this object carry?</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> These questions can also be asked of supernatural entities, allowing Frank to better expand his understanding. The glasses won\u2019t out and out say \u201cthis is a Werewolf\u201d, but they will give him the impressions of a phenomena and magical \u201cfingerprint\u201d that he can trace back to a werewolf when he sees other werewolf related things. With one of his successes he can also choose to spend a point of Plasm to activate the relic as if he had the proper mystical energy. (<i>For those with Mage: The Awakening second edition, this is a somewhat squishier and looser version of Supernal Vision and Word of Command, don\u2019t worry about the specifics</i>)<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Filcher\u2019s Eye (Silent Key):</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A creepy little eyeball that clearly isn't human attached to a leather bound book by a delicate chain. Hold the eye in your hand and whisper to it, then hold it out to a closed door\u2014even a supernatural one, so long as you're aware it exists\u2014and the dusty grey eye will regain color and sprout batlike wings and float through the door, the chain extending as long as it needs to. By giving the book a little bit of supernatural juice (plasm in Frank\u2019s case) the book will begin describing whatever the eye sees, including detailed sketches if necessary. Don\u2019t worry, if you can\u2019t provide supernatural ink, blood will do. Careful, though; if anyone else takes the book, they can see everything you\u2019ve scoped out. (<i>To find out more about Tokens, check out Changeling: The Lost second edition</i>)<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>The House Key (Beast Key):</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A heavy, rusty old key with feathers and claws dangling from the key chain. By walking an enclosed area, such as a house, and spending five plasm, Frank wards the area against intrusion. Anyone who would threaten him or his allies has to roll Wits+Survival-[Beast Key] to avoid gaining the Lost Condition. Space simply stretches, and doors lead back in on themselves. This effect lasts for a month, but can only be used on one location at a time. (<i>This is a Fetish from Werewolf: The Forsaken second edition that grants a simplified version of the Maze Ward facet of Warding Gifts; just go with it</i>)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And much like with Sabrina, there's a &quot;canon&quot; Geist for Frank. This one is another &quot;Strange Geist&quot; like I love so much. But things get weird when your Mage boyfriend deals with an Acamoth. Also while I love a good reference I will admit this one might be a little much. Then again, &quot;The Survivor&quot; is just Kelsier. <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1295_1688902498173_679\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1295\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1295\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1295&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spirits are alien things. The more advanced ones can take on strange forms with unusual connotations. The Detective on Leather Wings for instance is a spirit of investigation, particularly the kind of investigation you do in order to get revenge or vengeance or simply fuck over the right people. It feeds on the resonance of justified violence and the certainty that comes from tracking down a wrongdoer and seeing them punished. It also, for whatever reason, takes the form of a massive humanoid bat with fiery eyes. Sometimes it becomes more human, a hooded figure with wings wrapped around it like a cloak and a heavy high collar. Or maybe simply a demonic shadow on the ground where it\u2019s Bound stands.<br /> The Detective is yet another strange entity that found itself in the Underworld and drank from a River, and in doing so twisted its corpus into something capable of making the Bargain. It wants someone who will seek down wrongdoers and punish them. Or at the very least keep it entertained with the thrill of a puzzling foe. It communicates in broad gestures like Bengt Ekerot\u2019s Death, and the distant sound of night creatures screeching.<br /> <br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> The death of parents, a lifelong search for revenge, feeding on a life of vigilantism, finding its way to the Underworld<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Touchstone:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> A murder scene in an alleyway<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Remembrance Trait:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Investigation<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Power \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Finesse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Resistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Rank \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Virtue:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Determination; <b><b><b>Vice:</b></b></b> Determination<br /> <b><b><b><b>Ban:</b></b></b></b> Can\u2019t harm the innocent (but can scare the shit out of them), <b><b><b><b><b>Bane:</b></b></b></b></b> An innocent (such as a cultist or captive) attacking him<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Crisis Point:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Injustice, The Detective can\u2019t abide by harm being done in front of it, and woe be it if the Bound chooses to.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Burden:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Kindly, though the Detective was never alive, nor died.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Suggested Keys:</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b> Blood - They deserve it, Chance - One bad day can change everything, Silent - the sound of a predator, Cold Wind - nothing but the wind<br /> <br /> <b>Deathmask - The Cowl</b><br /> The Cowl is a terrifying balaclava looking leather hood and cloak with sharp points reminiscent of a bat\u2019s ears\u2014or the horns of a demon. When a ghost wears the Cowl it becomes the <b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b><b>Spirit of Vengeance</b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b></b>, a horrifying shadow that looks to punish ghosts for the crimes they did in life, brutalizing them when they resist. It Engulfs a ghost while it\u2019s broken, pouncing on it and covering it with the winglike cloak.<br /> <b><b><b><b><b><b>Quirk:</b></b></b></b></b></b> The Cowl is a tool of terror. Whether you use it on those who are deserving or not is up to the wearer. Any successful Intimidation action or any amount of damage against a target causes the Beaten Down Tilt by spending a point of Willpower.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 07-09-2023, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T11:27:50-07:00","id":1536371,"title":"","content":"This is incredible. I just got really into Geist and specifically googled if anyone was working on a Night Horrors type book for it. I think it would be really great, with the huge variety of living and dead creatures that could be added. And I love what you've done so far!! Great stuff!<br /> <br /> Are you still working on it? Is there anything I can do to help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28045-watt-grego","name":"Watt Grego","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T07:18:38-07:00","id":1536869,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to have a geist that's made up of multiple people combined into one being? Some examples could be:<br /> <br /> A group of soldiers who all died on the same mission.<br /> <br /> A group of genocide victims.<br /> <br /> People who committed group suicide.<br /> <br /> A group of plague victims.<br /> <br /> A group of couples who were killed because their relationships were illegal or taboo (e.g. Interracial couples, intercaste couples, same-sex couples)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T09:03:46-07:00","id":1536871,"title":"","content":"RAW? No. But if you think it would make a good story, go for it. I'm iffy on &quot;if it would make a good story&quot; for a lot of your list, but hey, you do you. <br /> <br /> That aside, I don't think OP's around any more, they seemed to have left the community when they left the discord almost a year ago so I fear these projects aren't being worked on any longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}